"output_tokens":5691.0,"requests":10}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the DC-cutover assertion: _issues.py uses a function `_description_codec()` (not `_DESCRIPTION_CODEC`) and already applies `to_wire(fit_outbound(...))` at line 123; restate which send site actually ships un-rendered Markdown (backend.py's `_map_local_to_dc_fields`, which fits without `to_wire`).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Grep '_DESCRIPTION_CODEC' → (no matches) across the whole repo","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:46-47 defines a FUNCTION `_description_codec()` returning WikiTextCodec(rich=...)","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:123: `fields[\"description\"] = codec.to_wire(codec.fit_outbound(description))` — already routes through to_wire","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:118-121 comment: 'CREATE is a SECOND DC send path ... It must render too: fitting without to_wire would post raw Markdown on create'","backend.py:72 (`_map_local_to_dc_fields`) IS the site that applies `codec.fit_outbound(...)` without to_wire"],"finding":"The DC-cutover section asserts _issues.py has an 'OWN _DESCRIPTION_CODEC [that] applied only fit_outbound WITHOUT to_wire' and therefore 'must route through to_wire (render before the fit) or [it] ship[s] un-rendered Markdown'. This is refuted by the code: no symbol named _DESCRIPTION_CODEC exists anywhere (grep returns no matches); _issues.py uses a function _description_codec() (line 46-47) and line 123 already executes codec.to_wire(codec.fit_outbound(description)) — it already renders before the fit. Only backend.py's _map_local_to_dc_fields (line 72) applies fit_outbound without to_wire.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe2653cec23efe224","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"The live cutover → DC: 'TWO other DC send sites: _map_local_to_dc_fields ... AND adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py, whose OWN